[standards/application/styling/STD-APP-UI-001-frontend-styling-standards.md#std-ui-003-no-arbitrary-value-overuse]

#### STD-UI-003: No Arbitrary Value Overuse

**SHOULD NOT** use Tailwind's arbitrary value syntax (`[value]`) for values that are already in the design token system or the default Tailwind scale.

```tsx
// ❌ NON-COMPLIANT — arbitrary value when a token class exists
<div className="bg-[hsl(210,84%,44%)]">...</div>

// ✅ COMPLIANT — semantic token class
<div className="bg-primary">...</div>

// ✅ PERMITTED — arbitrary value for a genuine one-off not in the scale
<div className="h-[3px]">...</div>  {/* hairline border-like separator */}
```

