[standards/application/styling/STD-APP-UI-001-frontend-styling-standards.md#std-ui-008-mobile-first-breakpoints]

#### STD-UI-008: Mobile-First Breakpoints

**MUST** apply base styles targeting mobile (no breakpoint prefix) first, then progressively enhance with ascending breakpoint prefixes. Do not use a desktop-first approach that requires overriding at smaller breakpoints.

```tsx
// ✅ COMPLIANT — mobile first, enhanced at md and lg
<div className="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">

// ❌ NON-COMPLIANT — desktop first (requires max-width workarounds not available in Tailwind)
<div className="grid grid-cols-3 gap-4">  {/* breaks on mobile — no override mechanism */}
```

