[standards/application/styling/STD-APP-UI-001-frontend-styling-standards.md#std-ui-012-global-css-limited-to-tokens-and-resets]

#### STD-UI-012: Global CSS Limited to Tokens and Resets

`globals.css` (or `app/globals.css` in Next.js) **MUST** contain only:

- CSS custom property definitions (design tokens — see GUID-APP-UI-001)
- Tailwind base/components/utilities directives
- Base resets or normalizations that cannot be achieved with Tailwind's `@layer base`
- Font face declarations

```css
/* globals.css — COMPLIANT structure */
/* Import the canonical enterprise design system — do NOT redefine tokens here */
@import '@mmes/cmn-core/components/react/core-theme.css';

@tailwind base;
@tailwind components;
@tailwind utilities;

@layer base {
  body {
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-family: var(--body-font-family);
    font-size: var(--font-size-regular);
    background: var(--background-primary);
  }
}
```

**Do NOT redefine token values in `globals.css`** — those are owned by `@mmes/cmn-core/core-theme.css`. Only application-specific additions (e.g. additional `@font-face` declarations not in core) may appear here.

> **Kendo UI co-existence exception (STD-UI-012-EX1):** When a module includes Kendo UI for React under the approved exception (§2.2, GUID-APP-TEC-003), Tailwind's global preflight reset **MUST** be disabled and scoped to a wrapper element to prevent Tailwind's universal selectors from breaking Kendo's internal DOM. Set `corePlugins: { preflight: false }` in `tailwind.config.ts` and apply scoped resets via a `.tw-root` wrapper class. See GUID-APP-TEC-003 § "Integration with Shadcn/UI + Tailwind CSS" for the required implementation pattern. This exception applies only to modules that include a Kendo component; all other modules **MUST** leave Tailwind preflight enabled.

