[standards/application/styling/STD-APP-UI-001-frontend-styling-standards.md#std-ui-017-token-level-contrast-validation]

#### STD-UI-017: Token-Level Contrast Validation

All semantic design token pairs defined in GUID-APP-UI-001 **MUST** be validated for contrast compliance before being merged. Use the following script pattern:

```typescript
// scripts/validate-contrast.ts
import { colord } from 'colord';
import { a11yPlugin } from 'colord/plugins/a11y';

colord.extend([a11yPlugin]);

// Use actual hex values from @mmes/cmn-core/core-theme.css
const tokenPairs = [
  { fg: '#2b3a44', bg: '#ffffff', label: 'text-primary / background-primary (light)' },
  { fg: '#ffffff', bg: '#0062ff', label: 'text-inverse / button-bg-primary (light)'  },
  { fg: '#d7385e', bg: '#ffffff', label: 'text-error / background-primary (light)'   },
  { fg: '#5a6978', bg: '#ffffff', label: 'text-secondary / background-primary (light)'},
  { fg: '#ffffff', bg: '#2b3a44', label: 'text-primary / background-primary (dark)'  },
];

for (const { fg, bg, label } of tokenPairs) {
  const ratio = colord(fg).contrast(colord(bg));
  if (ratio < 4.5) {
    console.error(`FAIL: ${label} — ratio ${ratio.toFixed(2)} < 4.5:1`);
    process.exit(1);
  }
  console.log(`PASS: ${label} — ratio ${ratio.toFixed(2)}:1`);
}
```

