[standards/application/styling/STD-APP-UI-001-frontend-styling-standards.md#std-ui-020-font-stack]

#### STD-UI-020: Font Stack

**MUST** use the enterprise font stack defined in `@mmes/cmn-core/core-theme.css` and mapped to Tailwind via `tailwind.config.ts`:

```css
/* Defined in core-theme.css */
--body-font-family:     Arial, "Helvetica Neue", Helvetica, sans-serif;
--headings-font-family: "Poppins Bold", Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
--font-family-monospace: monospace;
```

```typescript
// tailwind.config.ts
fontFamily: {
  sans:    ['Arial', '"Helvetica Neue"', 'Helvetica', 'sans-serif'],
  heading: ['"Poppins Bold"', 'Arial', 'Helvetica', 'sans-serif'],
  mono:    ['monospace'],
}
```

Apply `font-sans` on the `<body>` element; `font-heading` for headings; `font-mono` for code and technical identifiers. Do not use Inter or JetBrains Mono — those are not the enterprise font stack.

