[standards/application/styling/STD-APP-UI-001-frontend-styling-standards.md#std-ui-024-consume-core-themecss-tokens-for-standard-surfaces]

#### STD-UI-024: Consume `core-theme.css` Tokens for Standard Surfaces

**MUST** consume `@mmes/cmn-core/core-theme.css` semantic tokens (`--text-*`, `--background-*`, `--widget-*`, `--button-*`, `--border-*`, `--icon-*`, `--table-*`) directly for all standard UI surfaces. **MUST NOT** create per-module token aliases that duplicate what `core-theme.css` already provides.

```css
/* ✅ COMPLIANT — reads from core-theme.css */
.field-label  { color: var(--text-primary);  font-size: var(--widget-label-font-size); }
.field-input  { height: var(--widget-input-height); border: var(--widget-border); }
.field-error  { color: var(--text-error); border: var(--widget-error-border); }

/* ❌ NON-COMPLIANT — inventing per-module aliases for standard tokens */
.field-label  { color: var(--my-module-text, #2b3a44); }
.field-input  { border: var(--my-module-border, 1px solid #ced4da); }
```

Modules inherit light/dark theming automatically — the host shell applies `.theme-light` or `.theme-dark` and `core-theme.css` switches the token values. No module-level theme handling is required.

